    {
      "ordinal": 5,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "3.1",
      "title": "Material Requirements",
      "body": "All Tabards and Scarves must respect the following requirements:\n\n● Shapes, decorations and designs must be based on historical sources.\n● Tabards must conform to the “Textiles and Leather” document.\n● Tabards can be made of the following materials:\n\n○ wool, ○ linen, ○ silk,\n\n○ coton,\n\n○ any other material based on historical sources.\n\n● Tabards can be made of modern materials in the following cases:\n○ the modern material replicates the aesthetic of an approved material listed above, ○ the modern material is strong enough to endure full contact fights and to not be damaged too easily, ○ we recommend asking for approval of the Authenticity Committee regarding Tabard made of modern materials before placing an order.",
      "page_from": 4,
      "page_to": 4,
      "stable_key": "tabards:3.1",
      "parent_key": "tabards:3",
