    {
      "ordinal": 6,
      "depth": 1,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "3.2",
      "title": "Fastening Systems Requirements",
      "body": "Tabards can be tied with the following systems:\n\n● buttons made of fabric, wood, bone, or metal,\n\n● laces, made of leather, rope or fabric,\n\n● any other system based on historical sources,\n\n● any modern fastening system is denied. (Zips, snap buttons, velcro, paracord, nylon rope etc.).\n\nTabards can be open on the side, tied with laces.\nTabards can be open on the front, and tied with buttons.",
