      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "5.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "Short-sleeves Tabard is the main design of the 14th century and later. Its simple shape makes it easy to craft and to wear. Many different designs can be documented by historical sources\n\nThey are Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\n\nBible historiale - 1360 - France Weltchronik - 1360 - Germany Office of the Feast of Corpus Christi - 1403 - Austria",
