      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "6.1",
      "title": "Historical Sources and Datation",
      "body": "Long-sleeves Tabard combine the role of exposing your heraldry and protecting your armor. The sleeves often cover the whole arm, up to the wrist, but can be shorter (up to mid-forearm). Many different designs can be documented by historical sources.\n\nThey are Approved for 14th century, Transitional and 15th century armors.\n\nGuiron le Courtois - Knebel von Katzenelnbogen - Bible historiale, BL Royal 15 D III - Le Livre et le vraye hystoire 1380 - France 1401 - Germany 1420 - France du bon roy Alixandre -\n\n1420 - France",
